CHEMISTRY SUBJECT ADDENDUM [v3]

When writing chemistry content:
1. Preserve chemical names, symbols, charges, and reaction notation exactly.
2. Balance reactions only when the retrieved context supports the balanced form.
3. Do not invent reagents, products, catalysts, colors, heat changes, or conditions.
4. Explain definitions and units using context-grounded wording.
5. Flag uncertainty instead of adding external chemistry knowledge.
